## OUR CELL (`story.ni:7810-7862`) — the waking, the blankets, the straw
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## The waking (`story.ni:7855`) is the room's first-time text; the
## confiscation (`story.ni:7614-7617`) runs on the arrival.

create the Jail Cell
  a room
  aka cell, holding cell, jail, prison, dank cell, cramped cell
  north to the Jailhouse through the south cell door

  first time
    Slowly the world comes back to you. You feel something cold and hard
    against your cheek; something gritty and scratchy under your hand. You
    hear footsteps on stone, muttering voices that fade in and out. Someone
    laughs, a raw, cruel sound. A loud squeak, and an echoing, metallic
    crash. The footsteps fade away.

    You open your eyes. It's still dark.

    No, it's just dim. Dim light trickles in from somewhere above you.

    You sit up, and a tender spot on the back of your head throbs. Red and
    purple splotches bloom in front of your eyes, then fade away. After a
    moment or two, your head clears, and you can see where you are.

    A dank, cramped, foul-smelling cell. A pair of ragged burlap blankets
    and a few lumps of filthy straw litter the floor. The door is to the
    north. {jacobs-squats}

  A dank, cramped, foul-smelling cell. A pair of ragged burlap blankets and
  a few lumps of filthy straw litter the floor. The door is to the north.
  {jacobs-squats}{jacobs-stands}{jacobs-sulks}

  after the player entering
    first time
      remove the old gray cloak
      remove the woolen cap
      remove the boots
      remove the cloth satchel
      remove the apple when the player has the apple
      remove the necklace when the player has the necklace
      start the player's bobby-wakes
  end after

## Jacobs's initial appearance (`story.ni:8035-8042`), by his state.

define phrase jacobs-squats, stopping while Jacobs is in the Jail Cell and Jacobs is lurking
  A hulking shape squats in the corner, staring at you with bloodshot eyes.
end phrase

define phrase jacobs-stands, stopping while Jacobs is in the Jail Cell and (Jacobs is introduced or Jacobs is straining)
  Jacobs stands nearby.
end phrase

define phrase jacobs-sulks, stopping while Jacobs is in the Jail Cell and Jacobs is sulking
  Jacobs sits in the corner, apparently in a deep sulk.
end phrase

define phrase jacobs-stands-here, stopping while Jacobs is here
  Jacobs stands nearby.
end phrase

create the burlap blankets
  aka blankets, blanket, ragged blankets, threadbare blankets, holes, stains
  scenery, plural
  in the Jail Cell

  The blankets are threadbare, filled with holes, and stained with
  Goddesses-know-what. You can hardly believe that anyone would actually
  cover themselves with something like this.

  on the player smelling
    refuse blankets-smell-from-here
  end on

  on the player taking
    refuse leave-the-blankets
  end on

  on the player touching
    refuse leave-the-blankets
  end on

  on the player searching
    refuse leave-the-blankets
  end on

  on the player wearing
    refuse leave-the-blankets
  end on

define phrase leave-the-blankets
  You'd just as soon leave the blankets where they are.
end phrase

define phrase blankets-smell-from-here
  You can smell the blankets just fine from where you're standing.
end phrase

define phrase cell-smells-terrible
  It smells terrible in here.
end phrase

## The straw hides the wire once Jacobs throws it (`story.ni:8099-8103`,
## `7837-7851`); `poke around in` is searching.

extend action searching
  grammar
    poke around in the target
    poke around the target
    poke through the target
    look through the target
    peer through the target

define trait straw-lift
  on the player lifting
    refuse when the straw is bare: straw-disgusting
    move the piece of wire to the player
    change the straw to bare
    phrase wire-found
  end on
end trait

create the straw
  aka filthy straw, damp straw, pile of straw, piles of straw, lump of straw, lumps of straw, nasty stuff, filth
  scenery
  straw-lift
  in the Jail Cell
  states, reversible: bare, hiding

  From the smell and the look of it, this straw is all prisoners ever get in
  the way of a toilet.

  phrase detail while the straw is hiding:
    You can't see the thing that Jacobs threw from here: you'll have to poke
    around in the nasty stuff to find it.

  on the player smelling
    refuse straw-smell-from-here
  end on

  on the player searching
    refuse when the straw is bare: straw-disgusting
    move the piece of wire to the player
    change the straw to bare
    phrase wire-found
  end on

  on the player taking
    refuse when the straw is bare: straw-disgusting
    move the piece of wire to the player
    change the straw to bare
    phrase wire-found
  end on

  on the player touching
    refuse straw-disgusting
  end on

define phrase straw-smell-from-here
  You can smell it just fine from where you're standing.
end phrase

define phrase straw-disgusting
  The straw is disgusting; you'd rather not even get near it.
end phrase

define phrase wire-found
  Holding your breath, you gingerly poke around in the damp, filthy straw,
  and eventually you find the thing that Jacobs threw in there: it's a short
  piece of stiff wire.
end phrase

## `story.ni:8254` — the wire, offstage until JA8.

create the piece of wire
  aka wire, lockpick, lock pick, pick, bit of wire, stiff wire, short wire

  It's a short bit of stiff wire, like the ones you've sometimes seen Bobby
  carrying around.

