create the Jailhouse
  a room
  aka main room, jailhouse main room, guard room, crude room
  southwest to the Drain Room
  east is blocked: no-way-out-alone
  south is blocked: not-going-back-in
  north is blocked: not-going-back-in
  west is blocked: not-going-back-in
  states: quiet, deceiving

  The jailhouse is hardly more comfortable than the cells themselves, just a
  crude, small room of unfinished stone, with a wooden bench and table for
  the guards. Cells are south, west, and north. A foul smell comes from a
  tiny alcove to the southwest, and a passageway to the east leads out.
  {jacobs-stands-here}

  on every turn while the player is in the Jailhouse and Jacobs is here and Jacobs is freed and the Jailhouse is quiet
    phrase jacobs-ja16-stub
    start Jacobs's offering
    change the Jailhouse to deceiving
  end on

  after the player entering while Olmer is in the North Cell and the Drain Room is explored
    phrase olmer-ol2-stub
  end after

define phrase no-way-out-alone
  There are more guards out there, and you don't know the way. You'll never
  escape from this jail all by yourself.
end phrase

define phrase not-going-back-in, stopping
  It's such a huge relief just to be out of a jail cell; you definitely have
  no desire to get back into one.
or
  No, you'd rather stay out of jail cells for a while.
or
  You're not going back in there.
end phrase

