## JA22 (`story.ni:8017`), verbatim, for the rewrite — the death behind the
## offer, unreachable through a stub:
##   "'Smart kid,' Jacobs says, following you closely. You can hear the
##   other prisoner shouting something behind you, but soon their voices
##   fade as you hurry down the corridor, leaving the cells far behind you.
##   Jacobs leads you down dim, torchlit halls until you reach a wooden
##   door. Jacobs motions you to be silent, then puts his ear up to the
##   wood. After a moment he nods, opens the door, and then shoves you
##   through it into the next room.
##   Bright lantern-light blinds you, and when your eyes clear you see a
##   dozen men of the Lord's Guard standing in a semicircle around you...
##   and in the middle, the man in the red robes.
##   'Little mouse...' murmurs the man in the red robes, '...always finding
##   some new hole to crawl through.'
##   Behind you, Jacobs puts his heavy hand on your shoulder and grips it
##   tight. 'Like I said, runt,' he laughs, 'Fossville has taken a special
##   interest in you. And aiding the Baron in his interests can be very
##   profitable.'
##   The red-robed man and the guards close in on you. This time, you do
##   not escape."

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## OLMER AND DARRENS (`story.ni:8302-8452`)
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## OLMER SEES HER (change document, "Who sees her" — David: "A"): every
## "girl", "miss" and "young lady" below is a tell and carries verbatim.

create Olmer
  aka bald headed man, bald-headed man, bald man, red faced man, red-faced man, short man, drunkard, drunk, prisoner, prisoners, men
  a person, proper
  pronouns he
  in the North Cell
  states: nameless, named

  A short, bald-headed man, with a week's worth of stubble on his neck and a
  nose bright red from burst blood vessels. His breath reeks of cheap
  spirits, and his watery eyes shift constantly, as though always looking
  for a way out of his current predicament.

  when pleading expires, while Olmer is in the North Cell
    phrase olmer-ol1-stub
  end when

  on the player talking
    phrase olmer-ol10-stub when Olmer is in the Drain Room
    phrase olmer-ol9-stub when Olmer is in the North Cell
    change Olmer to named
  end on

create Darrens
  aka skinny man, tall man, scarecrow, wobbly man, mute, mute man, friend, associate
  a person, proper
  pronouns he
  in the North Cell

  He's a tall, wobbly scarecrow of a man, with a huge nose, ears like jug
  handles jutting from the sides of his head, and a throat-apple the size of
  a child's fist that bobs up and down constantly. He never speaks; just
  smiles and nods whenever anyone says or does anything. You suspect he may
  be a few coins short of a full purse.

  on the player talking
    phrase darrens-waggles when Olmer is named
    phrase skinny-man-waggles when Olmer is nameless
  end on

define phrase darrens-waggles
  Darrens just waggles his head and smiles at you.
end phrase

define phrase skinny-man-waggles
  The skinny man just waggles his head and smiles at you.
end phrase

define phrase olmer-ol1-stub
  (TODO during play-testing — conversation OL1: "'Do us a kindness, girl,
  and free us as well,' whines the man in the north cell. 'We ain't done
  nothin' terrible, and we can show you a way out, too, one that doesn't
  include leaving you dead in an alley for your shoes.'" — OL3/OL4/OL5:
  hang on, let them out, who are you. "Girl" is a tell: Olmer SEES her. The
  north door is hers to unlock.)
end phrase

define phrase olmer-ol2-stub
