  The thick bars of metal cover a rectangular hole that drops down into
  darkness. Around the edges of the grate, the stonework is loose and
  crumbling.
end phrase

define phrase grate-description-moved
  The metal grate is lying off to one side.
end phrase

define phrase grate-lifted
  It's a strain, but you're just barely able to lift the heavy grate and
  drop it to the side with a dull clang.
end phrase

define phrase grate-lifted-after-you
  It's a strain, but you're just barely able to lift the heavy grate and
  drop it to the side with a dull clang. Olmer smiles and gestures towards
  the foul-smelling hole. 'After you,' he wheezes.
end phrase

define phrase grate-too-heavy
  That grate is too heavy to carry anywhere, and you don't feel like lifting
  it again.
end phrase

create the loose stonework
  aka stonework, crumbling stonework, stone, stones, crumbly stone, loose stone
