## `story.ni:8650`, verbatim, in the pieces Chord can gate.

define phrase olmer-in-the-muck
  Olmer drops down into the muck next to you, followed by Darrens. 'Now
  then, miss, cast your eye at these glyphs here,' whispers Olmer. His voice
  echoes off into the blackness as he brushes the rough stone with his
  fingertips. 'These are marked down by such poor blokes as have to take
  refuge down here on a more regular basis. They tells you where the tunnels
  lead, if you but know their language.' Darrens nods in solemn agreement.
end phrase

define phrase olmer-points-north-red
  'To get back to your neighborhood, you'll want to follow the red, see?'
  Olmer points off down the north tunnel.
end phrase

