## `story.ni:8739`, verbatim.

define phrase lost-in-the-sewers
  Suddenly you find yourself in a tunnel where there are no symbols painted
  anywhere. You try to retrace your steps, but you must have taken a wrong
  turn somewhere, because now you can't find any symbols anywhere. All of
  the tunnels look alike; you are completely turned around and don't even
  know which direction you are stumbling in.

  The next tunnel you take leads you to an area with no vents — it is pitch
  black. You slip as you turn around and fall into the water. Something
  slick and wriggly brushes past your face, and you thrash to your feet.

  You can't see any light, anywhere. You don't know what direction you just
  came from. Cold, smelly water numbs your feet. Despair and paralyzing
  panic close in on you as you realize that you have no means of finding
  your way through this labyrinth.

  You are stuck down here, blind in the stinking blackness, forever.
end phrase

## The sewer backdrops (`story.ni:8571-8596`): followers, as the market's.

create the sewer water
  aka water, sewage, ooze, garbage, rats, dead rats, rat, muck, filth water
  scenery
  in the Sewer

  The water is sluggish and cold, knee-deep in most places. Things float
  past you in the ooze — garbage, dead rats, and worse. You try to avoid the
  worst of it, but it's already soaked through your shoes. You feel like
  you'll never be clean of it.

  when Jack moves, while the player is in the Sewers
    move the sewer water here
  end when

  on the player searching
    refuse makes-you-gag
  end on

  on the player drinking
    refuse makes-you-gag
  end on

  on the player smelling
    refuse makes-you-gag
  end on

  on the player touching
    refuse soaked-through
  end on

define phrase makes-you-gag
  The thought makes you gag.
end phrase

define phrase soaked-through
  You can't help touching it — it's soaked through your clothes.
end phrase

create the ancient bricks
  aka bricks, brick, walls, wall, tunnel walls, slimy bricks, slime, mold, unmortared brick
  scenery, plural
  in the Sewer

  The tunnel walls are slimy with filth and mold.

  when Jack moves, while the player is in the Sewers
    move the ancient bricks here
  end when

  on the player climbing
    refuse no-foothold
  end on

  on the player touching
    refuse rather-not-touch-the-walls
  end on

  on the player smelling
    refuse rather-not-touch-the-walls
  end on

  on the player eating
    refuse rather-not-touch-the-walls
  end on

define phrase no-foothold
  You can't get a foothold on the slimy bricks.
end phrase

define phrase rather-not-touch-the-walls
  You'd rather not touch the walls at all.
end phrase

create the ceiling vents
  aka vents, vent, grating, gratings, light, dim light, trickle of light, ceiling
  scenery, plural
  in the Sewer

  The ceiling vents let in a tiny trickle of light, barely enough to see by.

  when Jack moves, while the player is in the Sewers
    move the ceiling vents here
  end when

  on the player taking
    refuse vents-out-of-reach
  end on

  on the player touching
    refuse vents-out-of-reach
  end on

  on the player climbing
    refuse vents-out-of-reach
  end on

  on the player entering
